<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY THREE-MONTH BILL YIELD FALLS TO 20.61 PCT.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY THREE-MONTH BILL YIELD FALLS TO 20.61 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the</p>
<p>latest issue of three-month discount treasury bills was set by</p>
<p>auction at 20.61 percent, down from 20.71 percent at an auction</p>
<p>one week ago, the Government Debt Management Centre said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     13,347.80 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average yield		     20.61 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     95.1127 pct</p>
</text>
